Name who asked a window to miniaturize.

A window that believes it is miniaturized never updates its frame again:
-platformWindow:frameChanged:didSize: skips the assignment for a miniaturized window, so every
later resize reads back the old size, the backing bitmap is grown to hold a window that is no
longer that big, and the compositor is shown the wrong rows of it. From outside that looks exactly
like a resize defect.

It reached that state with the window MAIN, KEY and VISIBLE, and as its own sender, so the caller
was the whole question and no state dump could answer it. The backtrace named it in one run:

    CIDER_MINI miniaturize: window=0x7087febf1a00 sender=iTermWindow
    CIDER_MINI   AppKit    -[NSApplication sendAction:to:from:]
    CIDER_MINI   AppKit    -[NSMenu performKeyEquivalent:]
    CIDER_MINI   iTerm2    -[PTYTextView performKeyEquivalent:]

which is the Minimize item matching a Command M that the harness sent by accident. So the trace
earned its place by exonerating the port rather than by finding a defect in it, and it stays
because the next window that miniaturizes itself will raise the same question.

Gated on CIDER_TRACE_MINIATURIZE, and miniaturize: is rare enough that a getenv per call costs
nothing.

Task #252.

--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -3735,6 +3735,28 @@
 }
 
 - (void) miniaturize: (id) sender {
+    /* WHO ASKED. A window that believes it is miniaturized never updates its frame again, because
+     * -platformWindow:frameChanged:didSize: skips the assignment for a miniaturized window, and
+     * that leaves every later resize stale. iTerm2 reaches this with the window as its own sender
+     * while it is main, key and visible, so the caller is the whole question. Task #252. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_MINIATURIZE") != NULL) {
+        void *frames[24];
+        int count = backtrace(frames, 24);
+
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_MINI miniaturize: window=%p sender=%s\n", self,
+                sender != nil ? object_getClassName(sender) : "(nil)");
+        for (int i = 1; i < count; i++) {
+            Dl_info info;
+
+            if (dladdr(frames[i], &info) != 0 && info.dli_sname != NULL) {
+                const char *image = info.dli_fname ? strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/') : NULL;
+
+                fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_MINI   %-26s %s\n", image ? image + 1 : "?",
+                        info.dli_sname);
+            }
+        }
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
     [[self cider_platformWindow] miniaturize];
 }
 
